        "original_id": "a223f46a-7367-5944-8fe5-674a1036c6d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Marcus Welby, M.D.\n- People: Robert Young, James Brolin, Elena Verdugo, Josh Brolin, Barbra Streisand\n- Roles: Marcus Welby, Steve Kiley, Consuelo Lopez\n- Companies: ABC\n\nFacts:\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. was an American medical drama television program that aired on ABC on Tuesdays from 10:00 to 11:00 p.m. EST from September 23, 1969 to July 29, 1976.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred Robert Young as Marcus Welby, a family practitioner known for a kind bedside manner, close relationships with patients, and making house calls.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred James Brolin as Steve Kiley, a younger doctor who was Welby’s partner.\n- Marcus Welby, M.D. starred Elena Verdugo as Consuelo Lopez, the dedicated nurse and office manager for Welby and Kiley.\n- James Brolin was born Craig Kenneth Bruderlin on July 18, 1940.\n- James Brolin is an American actor, producer, and director known for film and television roles, including sitcoms and soap operas.\n- James Brolin is the father of actor Josh Brolin and the husband of singer and actress Barbra Streisand.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
